            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "@pkazmier I think this can even be simplified by passing an array of patterns for the keyword + the colon \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a3f274633a57c713160baf51724ecfc051117877/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L273-L274 \r\n\r\nUpdate: ignore this, it won't work in your case.\r\n\r\nHere is what I'm doing (_I now it can be simplified, still didn't make up my mind on highlighting the whole line or not_)\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal hipatterns = require 'mini.hipatterns'\r\n\r\nlocal highlighters = {}\r\nfor _, word in ipairs {\r\n\t'todo',\r\n\t'note',\r\n\t'hack',\r\n\t'fixme',\r\n\t{ 'warn', 'hack' },\r\n\t{ 'bug', 'fixme' },\r\n} do\r\n\tlocal w = type(word) == 'table' and word[1] or word\r\n\tlocal hl = type(word) == 'table' and word[2] or word\r\n\r\n\thighlighters[w] = {\r\n\t\tpattern = {\r\n\t\t\tstring.format('()@%s()', w:upper()),\r\n\t\t\tstring.format('()%s()', w:upper()),\r\n\t\t\tstring.format('%s():()', w:upper()),\r\n\t\t\tstring.format('%s ().*()', w:upper()),\r\n\t\t\tstring.format('%s: ().*()', w:upper()),\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t\tgroup = string.format(\r\n\t\t\t'MiniHipatterns%s',\r\n\t\t\thl:sub(1, 1):upper() .. hl:sub(2)\r\n\t\t),\r\n\t}\r\nend\r\n\r\nhipatterns.setup {\r\n\thighlighters = vim.tbl_extend('force', highlighters, {\r\n\t\t-- Highlight hex color strings (`#rrggbb`) using that color\r\n\t\thex_color = hipatterns.gen_highlighter.hex_color(),\r\n\t}),\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nlooks like this \r\n\r\n<img width=\"370\" alt=\"Screenshot 2024-06-22 at 13 27 31\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/63876/c3ec57c1-f553-4768-84d8-2ef125c0b7be\">\r\n",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/pkazmier/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/pkazmier\">@pkazmier</a> I think this can even be simplified by passing an array of patterns for the keyword + the colon</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a3f274633a57c713160baf51724ecfc051117877/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L273-L274\">https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a3f274633a57c713160baf51724ecfc051117877/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L273-L274</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update: ignore this, it won't work in your case.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here is what I'm doing (<em>I now it can be simplified, still didn't make up my mind on highlighting the whole line or not</em>)</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local hipatterns = require 'mini.hipatterns'\n\nlocal highlighters = {}\nfor _, word in ipairs {\n\t'todo',\n\t'note',\n\t'hack',\n\t'fixme',\n\t{ 'warn', 'hack' },\n\t{ 'bug', 'fixme' },\n} do\n\tlocal w = type(word) == 'table' and word[1] or word\n\tlocal hl = type(word) == 'table' and word[2] or word\n\n\thighlighters[w] = {\n\t\tpattern = {\n\t\t\tstring.format('()@%s()', w:upper()),\n\t\t\tstring.format('()%s()', w:upper()),\n\t\t\tstring.format('%s():()', w:upper()),\n\t\t\tstring.format('%s ().*()', w:upper()),\n\t\t\tstring.format('%s: ().*()', w:upper()),\n\t\t},\n\t\tgroup = string.format(\n\t\t\t'MiniHipatterns%s',\n\t\t\thl:sub(1, 1):upper() .. hl:sub(2)\n\t\t),\n\t}\nend\n\nhipatterns.setup {\n\thighlighters = vim.tbl_extend('force', highlighters, {\n\t\t-- Highlight hex color strings (`#rrggbb`) using that color\n\t\thex_color = hipatterns.gen_highlighter.hex_color(),\n\t}),\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">hipatterns</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.hipatterns<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">highlighters</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {}\n<span class=\"pl-k\">for</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">_</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">word</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">in</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">ipairs</span> {\n\t<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>todo<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n\t<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>note<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n\t<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>hack<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n\t<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>fixme<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n\t{ <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>warn<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>hack<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n\t{ <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>bug<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>fixme<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n} <span class=\"pl-k\">do</span>\n\t<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">w</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">type</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">word</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>table<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">word</span>[<span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>] <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">word</span>\n\t<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">hl</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">type</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">word</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>table<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">word</span>[<span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span>] <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">word</span>\n\n\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">highlighters</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">w</span>] <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n\t\t\t<span class=\"pl-c1\">string.format</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>()@%s()<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-en\">w</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">upper</span>()),\n\t\t\t<span class=\"pl-c1\">string.format</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>()%s()<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-en\">w</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">upper</span>()),\n\t\t\t<span class=\"pl-c1\">string.format</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%s():()<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-en\">w</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">upper</span>()),\n\t\t\t<span class=\"pl-c1\">string.format</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%s ().*()<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-en\">w</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">upper</span>()),\n\t\t\t<span class=\"pl-c1\">string.format</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%s: ().*()<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-en\">w</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">upper</span>()),\n\t\t},\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">group</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">string.format</span>(\n\t\t\t<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>MiniHipatterns%s<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n\t\t\t<span class=\"pl-en\">hl</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">sub</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>, <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>):<span class=\"pl-c1\">upper</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">hl</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">sub</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span>)\n\t\t),\n\t}\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">hipatterns</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span> {\n\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">highlighters</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">tbl_extend</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>force<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">highlighters</span>, {\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Highlight hex color strings (`#rrggbb`) using that color</span>\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">hex_color</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">hipatterns</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_highlighter</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">hex_color</span>(),\n\t}),\n}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">looks like this</p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/63876/341965089-c3ec57c1-f553-4768-84d8-2ef125c0b7be.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..Xotwck3i4CuecpyL178gd5oOJSn5dEs6EPheFlAQIOw\"><img width=\"370\" alt=\"Screenshot 2024-06-22 at 13 27 31\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/63876/341965089-c3ec57c1-f553-4768-84d8-2ef125c0b7be.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..Xotwck3i4CuecpyL178gd5oOJSn5dEs6EPheFlAQIOw\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a>",
            "bodyText": "@pkazmier I think this can even be simplified by passing an array of patterns for the keyword + the colon\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a3f274633a57c713160baf51724ecfc051117877/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L273-L274\nUpdate: ignore this, it won't work in your case.\nHere is what I'm doing (I now it can be simplified, still didn't make up my mind on highlighting the whole line or not)\nlocal hipatterns = require 'mini.hipatterns'\n\nlocal highlighters = {}\nfor _, word in ipairs {\n\t'todo',\n\t'note',\n\t'hack',\n\t'fixme',\n\t{ 'warn', 'hack' },\n\t{ 'bug', 'fixme' },\n} do\n\tlocal w = type(word) == 'table' and word[1] or word\n\tlocal hl = type(word) == 'table' and word[2] or word\n\n\thighlighters[w] = {\n\t\tpattern = {\n\t\t\tstring.format('()@%s()', w:upper()),\n\t\t\tstring.format('()%s()', w:upper()),\n\t\t\tstring.format('%s():()', w:upper()),\n\t\t\tstring.format('%s ().*()', w:upper()),\n\t\t\tstring.format('%s: ().*()', w:upper()),\n\t\t},\n\t\tgroup = string.format(\n\t\t\t'MiniHipatterns%s',\n\t\t\thl:sub(1, 1):upper() .. hl:sub(2)\n\t\t),\n\t}\nend\n\nhipatterns.setup {\n\thighlighters = vim.tbl_extend('force', highlighters, {\n\t\t-- Highlight hex color strings (`#rrggbb`) using that color\n\t\thex_color = hipatterns.gen_highlighter.hex_color(),\n\t}),\n}\nlooks like this",
